      "name": "How much does it cost to replace a Toyota hybrid battery?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Toyota hybrid battery replacement cost typically ranges from $2,000 to $5,000, depending on the model and region."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I drive my Toyota hybrid with a bad battery?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It’s not recommended. A failing battery can reduce fuel efficiency, power, and overall performance, potentially causing long-term damage."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does a Prius hybrid battery last compared to other Toyota hybrids?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A Prius hybrid battery generally lasts around 8 to 10 years, similar to other Toyota hybrid models. However, due to its lightweight design, it may perform slightly better over time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can the Toyota hybrid battery be repaired instead of replaced?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
